  "n": 43,
  "title": "The Sleeping Dragon Debates the Scholars of Wu",
  "year": "208",
  "summary": [
    "Zhuge Liang crosses to Chaisang with nothing to offer and one thing to sell: the idea that Sun Quan can fight. Zhang Zhao and the civil officers, who want to surrender and keep their offices, take him apart one at a time in open court, and he answers all of them.",
    "He then goes to Sun Quan and does not argue at all. He observes that if Wu cannot fight, Wu should certainly surrender — and watches the young man's face change."
  ],
  "history": "The embassy is historical; the debate is the novel's finest set-piece and almost entirely invented.",
